cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, cite the repository. It currently documents a research harness, not a validated empirical result."
title: "Where Does Document Understanding Break? A Counterfactual Error-Propagation Study of OCR and OCR-Free VLMs"
abstract: >-
  A research harness for counterfactual, architecture-specific attribution of
  document question answering failures on multilingual documents. The repository
  implements a measurement protocol, metrics, routing experiments, and
  reproducibility tooling. As of version 0.1.0 it does not contain an executed
  confirmatory study; see docs/peer_review.md for the assessment.
authors:
  - family-names: "sidg2hp"
    name: "sidg2hp"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sidg2hp/Multilingual-document-QA-failure-analysis"
keywords:
  - document question answering
  - OCR
  - vision-language models
  - multilingual
  - error attribution
  - Indic scripts
